   485                                      ; 01h, 03h and 06h-08h are IBM POST-internal continuations whose
   486                                      ; scratch-frame layouts belong to the exact ROM revision that emitted
   487                                      ; them.  This clean-room BIOS never emits those values.  If stale CMOS or
   488                                      ; foreign firmware leaves one behind, clear it and perform a complete POST
   489                                      ; rather than interpreting alien private RAM as a return frame.  0Dh-FFh
   490                                      ; are likewise defined as ordinary startup by later AT-compatible BIOSes.
