  1452                                  .wait:
  1453                                      ; With IRQ1 enabled the interrupt handler may consume FAh/FEh before this
  1454                                      ; foreground command path observes port 64h.  INT 09h records that physical
  1455                                      ; response in BDA_KBD_STATUS4.  Honor the ISR-owned observation both before
  1456                                      ; and after the bounded OBF wait; otherwise a successful EDh can time out
  1457                                      ; after its ACK and leave the real keyboard waiting for its parameter with
  1458                                      ; scanning suspended.  Do not CLI around the transaction: an edge-triggered
  1459                                      ; IRQ1 would remain pending after a polled read and deliver a false empty-OBF
  1460                                      ; interrupt when FLAGS were restored.
